===BODY===
          <h2>The A500, the D Road</h2>
          <p>The A500 runs through Stoke-on-Trent from <a href="{{R}}routes/m6.html">M6</a> junction 15 in the south to junction 16 in the north. Locals call it the D Road because of its shape. It's a fast dual carriageway with short slip roads, and much of the city's traffic uses it. If your car starts to struggle on the A500, take the next exit rather than stopping on the narrow verge. If you can't, hazards on, get behind the barrier and call us with your direction and the last junction.</p>

          <h2>The A50 and the M6</h2>
          <p>The A50 leaves the A500 and heads east towards Uttoxeter and Derby. At the southern end of the city, junction 15 of the M6 is close to Trentham, and at the northern end junction 16 leads towards Crewe and Nantwich. Both junctions see heavy freight traffic, so tell us which side of the roundabout you're on and which way you were going.</p>

          <h2>The six towns</h2>
          <p>Tunstall, Burslem, Hanley, Stoke, Fenton and Longton each have their own centre and car parks. Hanley is the main shopping centre, with multi-storey car parks that often have low height limits. Tell us the town and the street, or the name of the car park and the level, and the driver will know what to bring. We also cover Newcastle-under-Lyme and Kidsgrove next door.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Broken down on the A500, the A50 or the M6?</strong> Get as far left as you can and put your hazards on. If it's safe, get out by the left-hand door and stand behind the barrier. If you can't, stay in the car with your seatbelt on and call 999. Then call us with the road, the nearest junction and your direction.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Hospitals, stadium and Trentham</h2>
          <p>If your car won't start at Royal Stoke University Hospital, give us the car park and level. On match days around the bet365 Stadium and at busy weekends at Trentham, the roads nearby fill up, so allow extra time and tell us the exact spot.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: My car has broken down on the A500. What do I do?
A: Take the next exit if you can. If not, hazards on, get behind the barrier and call us with your direction and the last junction.
Q: Do you cover Newcastle-under-Lyme and Kidsgrove?
A: Yes, as well as all six towns of Stoke-on-Trent.
Q: My car is in a multi-storey in Hanley. Can you get it out?
A: Usually, but low height limits sometimes mean the car has to be rolled to the exit first. Tell us the car park and level.
